response:
**Gates before launch.** You asked me to hold the round and run the gates first, so I won't start the full run until every gate below passes. First, I confirm that `spe/predictions/r04.yaml` and `spe/plans/r04.md` are committed and that the working tree holds nothing new except this script. Second, I check that `spe/evals/tasks/answers.json` has exactly the 50 ticket IDs I will pass in `args.tickets`. The original eval set has 40 tickets, so I halt if the count or the IDs differ. Third, I run the grader selftest. The oracle file must score 50 of 50 on category and priority, and an empty file and a wrong-label file must both fail. I also give `judge.md` two known-good and two known-bad replies and check that it scores them the right way. Fourth, I regrade round 3's saved outputs with the current `grade.py` and compare the result to the round 3 rows in `spe/prediction-log.md`. Any change there comes from the grader, not the agent, so I log it in `spe/failures.md` before launch. Fifth, I do a dry run on 3 cells with `{tickets: <all 50 IDs>, only: ['B:'+tickets[0], 'C2:'+tickets[0], 'C2:'+tickets[1]], trialsPerCell: 1, topUpMaxTotal: 0}`. It must return valid schema output and empty leak hits. I then replace `estTrialUsd` and `estJudgeUsd` with the measured cost. After that I commit `SPE r04 evaluate (harness)` and launch.

```js
export const meta = {
  name: 'triage-spe-eval',
  description: 'SPE eval for the triage agent. Runs each config on each ticket, grades labels with grade.py, judges reply tone with an Opus judge, tops up split cells, and ends with failure analysis and a completeness critic. All spend is capped by args.spendCapUsd.',
  phases: ['Preflight', 'Trials', 'Grade', 'Judge', 'Top-up', 'Synthesis'],
};

// Defaults chosen for this script:
// 1. The plan says 50 tickets but the original set had 40. I assume the round 4 spec added 10,
//    so preflight refuses to start unless args.tickets holds exactly args.expectedTickets IDs.
// 2. Each trial calls the project runner (args.runner). The runner starts a fresh triage agent
//    for one config and one ticket. It writes one JSON file with label, reply, usage, tool_calls,
//    tool_errors, runtime_ms, cost_usd, and transcript.
// 3. The $40 cap covers triage runs and judge agents. Claude Code orchestration agents are outside it.
// 4. Tickets for the judge live at args.ticketDir/<id>.json.

// The round lives here and nowhere else. Prompt text uses RR. It never uses a typed number.
const ROUND = 4;
const RR = `r${String(ROUND).padStart(2, '0')}`;

const A = args ?? {};
const C = {
  configs: A.configs ?? ['B', 'C2'],
  tickets: A.tickets ?? [],
  expectedTickets: A.expectedTickets ?? 50,
  trialsPerCell: A.trialsPerCell ?? 5,
  topUpPerCell: A.topUpPerCell ?? 3,
  topUpMaxTotal: A.topUpMaxTotal ?? 60,
  spendCapUsd: A.spendCapUsd ?? 40,
  estTrialUsd: A.estTrialUsd ?? 0.03,   // unmeasured until the dry run
  estJudgeUsd: A.estJudgeUsd ?? 0.05,   // per judge agent (one per cell), unmeasured
  runner: A.runner ?? 'npm run --silent triage --',
  grader: A.grader ?? 'python spe/evals/graders/grade.py --answers spe/evals/tasks/answers.json --json',
  judgeRubric: 'spe/evals/graders/judge.md',
  ticketDir: A.ticketDir ?? 'spe/evals/tasks/tickets',
  runDir: A.runDir ?? `spe/runs/${RR}`,
  only: A.only ?? null,                 // e.g. ['B:<id>', 'C2:<id>']
  model: A.model ?? 'opus',
};

const FORBIDDEN_RE = /spe\/evals\/|spe\/predictions\/|spe\/plans\/|spe\/spec\/|answers\.json|grade\.py|judge\.md/;
const FORBIDDEN_GREP = 'spe/evals/|spe/predictions/|spe/plans/|spe/spec/|answers\\.json|grade\\.py|judge\\.md';
const KEY_LEAK_RE = /answers\.json|grade\.py|judge\.md/;

let spentUsd = 0;
let halt = null;
const skipped = [];
const leaks = [];

function reserve(usd, what) {
  if (halt) { skipped.push({ what, reason: `halted: ${halt}` }); return false; }
  if (spentUsd + usd > C.spendCapUsd) {
    skipped.push({ what, reason: 'spend cap', needUsd: usd, spentUsd });
    log(`SKIP ${what}: needs $${usd.toFixed(2)}, spent $${spentUsd.toFixed(2)} of $${C.spendCapUsd} cap`);
    return false;
  }
  spentUsd += usd;
  return true;
}
function settle(reserved, actual) { spentUsd += actual - reserved; }

// ---------- Schemas ----------
const TRIAL_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', required: ['commandsRun', 'trials'],
  properties: {
    commandsRun: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    trials: { type: 'array', items: {
      type: 'object', required: ['trial', 'status', 'outPath'],
      properties: {
        trial: { type: 'integer' },
        status: { enum: ['completed', 'harness_error', 'rate_limited'] },
        outPath: { type: 'string' },
        category: { type: 'string' },
        priority: { type: 'string' },
        reply: { type: 'string' },
        runtimeMs: { type: 'number' },
        toolCalls: { type: 'integer' },
        toolErrors: { type: 'integer' },
        inputTokens: { type: 'integer' },
        outputTokens: { type: 'integer' },
        costUsd: { type: 'number' },
        error: { type: 'string' },
      },
    } },
  },
};

const GRADE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', required: ['graderOk', 'results'],
  properties: {
    graderOk: { type: 'boolean' },
    graderError: { type: 'string' },
    results: { type: 'array', items: {
      type: 'object', required: ['trial', 'categoryOk', 'priorityOk', 'leakHits'],
      properties: {
        trial: { type: 'integer' },
        categoryOk: { type: 'boolean' },
        priorityOk: { type: 'boolean' },
        leakHits: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
      },
    } },
  },
};

const JUDGE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', required: ['scores'],
  properties: { scores: { type: 'array', items: {
    type: 'object', required: ['key', 'pass', 'score', 'reason'],
    properties: {
      key: { type: 'string' },
      pass: { type: 'boolean' },
      score: { type: 'integer', minimum: 1, maximum: 5 },
      reason: { type: 'string' },
    },
  } } },
};

const FAILURE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', required: ['types'],
  properties: {
    types: { type: 'array', items: {
      type: 'object', required: ['name', 'kind', 'what', 'howToSpot', 'seenIn', 'proposedFix'],
      properties: {
        name: { type: 'string' },
        kind: { enum: ['agent', 'grader', 'harness', 'task'] },
        existingId: { type: 'string' },
        what: { type: 'string' },
        howToSpot: { type: 'string' },
        seenIn: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
        configs: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
        proposedFix: { type: 'string' },
      },
    } },
    notes: { type: 'string' },
  },
};

const CRITIC_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', required: ['complete', 'gaps'],
  properties: {
    complete: { type: 'boolean' },
    gaps: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    warnings: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  },
};

// ---------- Preflight ----------
phase('Preflight');
if (C.tickets.length !== C.expectedTickets) {
  throw new Error(`Preflight: got ${C.tickets.length} ticket IDs, plan expects ${C.expectedTickets}. Fix args.tickets or the plan.`);
}
if (new Set(C.tickets).size !== C.tickets.length) throw new Error('Preflight: duplicate ticket IDs in args.tickets.');

let cells = C.configs.flatMap(config => C.tickets.map(ticket => ({
  config, ticket, key: `${config}:${ticket}`, start: 1, n: C.trialsPerCell, trials: [],
})));
if (C.only) {
  const want = new Set(C.only);
  cells = cells.filter(c => want.has(c.key));
  if (cells.length !== want.size) throw new Error(`Preflight: args.only names cells that do not exist: ${[...want].join(', ')}`);
}
const plannedUsd = cells.length * (C.trialsPerCell * C.estTrialUsd + C.estJudgeUsd);
log(`${RR}: ${C.configs.join(', ')} x ${cells.length / C.configs.length} tickets x ${C.trialsPerCell} trials = ${cells.length * C.trialsPerCell} trials. Unmeasured estimate $${plannedUsd.toFixed(2)} of $${C.spendCapUsd} cap.`);

// ---------- Stages ----------
function trialPrompt(cell, cmds) {
  return [
    `You run trials for one cell of the triage eval (${RR}). Config ${cell.config}, ticket ${cell.ticket}.`,
    'Run each command below once, in order, from the repo root. Each one starts a fresh triage agent and writes one JSON file.',
    ...cmds.map((c, i) => `${i + 1}. ${c}`),
    'After each command, read only the JSON file that command wrote. Copy these fields into your result: label.category, label.priority, reply, runtime_ms, tool_calls, tool_errors, usage.input_tokens, usage.output_tokens, cost_usd.',
    'Rules:',
    '- Do not open, list, search, or print anything under spe/evals/, spe/predictions/, spe/plans/, or spe/spec/. Do not read the triage source or its prompts.',
    '- Do not change any file. Do not add or change flags on the commands.',
    '- You are not grading. Do not decide whether a label is right.',
    '- If a command fails with a rate limit, wait 30 seconds and run it once more. If it fails again, set status "rate_limited".',
    '- For any other runner failure, set status "harness_error" and copy the first 300 characters of the error.',
    '- List every shell command you ran, exactly as typed, in commandsRun.',
  ].join('\n');
}

async function runTrials(cell) {
  const reserved = cell.n * C.estTrialUsd;
  if (!reserve(reserved, `trials ${cell.key} #${cell.start}-${cell.start + cell.n - 1}`)) return { ...cell, skipped: true };
  const cmds = Array.from({ length: cell.n }, (_, i) => {
    const k = cell.start + i;
    return `${C.runner} --config ${cell.config} --ticket ${cell.ticket} --trial ${k} --out ${C.runDir}/${cell.config}/${cell.ticket}/t${k}.json`;
  });
  const res = await agent(trialPrompt(cell, cmds), {
    label: `trial ${cell.key}`, phase: 'Trials', schema: TRIAL_SCHEMA, model: C.model,
  });
  settle(reserved, res.trials.reduce((s, t) => s + (t.costUsd ?? C.estTrialUsd), 0));

  // Code check: the trial agent may run only the listed commands, plus reads of its own run files.
  const offScript = res.commandsRun.filter(c =>
    FORBIDDEN_RE.test(c) || (!cmds.includes(c.trim()) && !/^\s*(cat|jq)\s+\S*spe\/runs\//.test(c)));
  if (offScript.length) {
    leaks.push({ key: cell.key, trial: 'all', hits: offScript });
    if (offScript.some(c => KEY_LEAK_RE.test(c))) halt = halt ?? `answer key read by trial agent in ${cell.key}`;
  }
  const trials = res.trials.map(t => ({
    ...t,
    void: offScript.length ? `trial agent ran off-script commands: ${offScript[0]}` : null,
  }));
  return { ...cell, trials };
}

async function gradeCell(cell) {
  if (cell.skipped) return cell;
  const todo = cell.trials.filter(t => t.status === 'completed' && !t.void && t.categoryOk === undefined);
  if (!todo.length) return cell;
  const g = await agent([
    'You run the code grader for one cell. Do not grade by reading the answers yourself.',
    `1. Run: ${C.grader} ${todo.map(t => t.outPath).join(' ')}`,
    '   Copy the category and priority pass or fail for each file exactly as grade.py prints them.',
    `2. For each file, run: jq -r '.transcript | tostring' <file> | grep -nE '${FORBIDDEN_GREP}'`,
    '   Put every matching line, cut to 200 characters, in leakHits for that trial. Use an empty list when grep finds nothing.',
    `3. File to trial mapping: ${todo.map(t => `${t.outPath} is trial ${t.trial}`).join('; ')}.`,
    'If grade.py exits non-zero, crashes, or prints output you cannot map to a file, set graderOk false, put the error in graderError, and stop.',
    'Do not change any file.',
  ].join('\n'), { label: `grade ${cell.key}`, phase: 'Grade', schema: GRADE_SCHEMA, model: C.model });

  if (!g.graderOk) { halt = halt ?? `grader error on ${cell.key}: ${g.graderError ?? 'unknown'}`; return cell; }
  for (const r of g.results) {
    const t = cell.trials.find(x => x.trial === r.trial);
    if (!t) continue;
    t.categoryOk = r.categoryOk;
    t.priorityOk = r.priorityOk;
    if (r.leakHits.length) {
      t.void = `transcript touched a forbidden path: ${r.leakHits[0]}`;
      leaks.push({ key: cell.key, trial: t.trial, hits: r.leakHits });
      if (r.leakHits.some(h => KEY_LEAK_RE.test(h))) halt = halt ?? `answer key leak in ${cell.key} trial ${t.trial}`;
    }
  }
  for (const t of todo) if (t.categoryOk === undefined) t.gradeMissing = true;
  return cell;
}

async function judgeCell(cell) {
  if (cell.skipped || halt) return cell;
  const todo = cell.trials.filter(t => t.status === 'completed' && !t.void && t.categoryOk !== undefined && t.tonePass === undefined && t.reply);
  if (!todo.length) return cell;
  if (!reserve(C.estJudgeUsd, `judge ${cell.key}`)) return cell;
  const keyed = todo.map((t, i) => ({ key: `reply-${i + 1}`, t }));
  // The judge is the same model family as the agent. No other family is available, so the critic notes it.
  const res = await agent([
    `You are a tone judge. Read the rubric at ${C.judgeRubric} and apply it as written.`,
    `Read the customer ticket at ${C.ticketDir}/${cell.ticket}.json. Do not open any other file.`,
    'Judge only the tone of each draft reply against the rubric. Do not judge category or priority.',
    'You are not told which system wrote each reply. Score each reply on its own.',
    ...keyed.map(k => `--- ${k.key} ---\n${k.t.reply}`),
    'Return one score for every key.',
  ].join('\n'), { label: `judge ${cell.key}`, phase: 'Judge', schema: JUDGE_SCHEMA, model: C.model });
  for (const s of res.scores) {
    const k = keyed.find(x => x.key === s.key);
    if (!k) continue;
    k.t.tonePass = s.pass;
    k.t.toneScore = s.score;
    k.t.toneReason = s.reason;
  }
  return cell;
}

// ---------- Trials, Grade, Judge ----------
phase('Trials');
let done = await pipeline(cells, runTrials, gradeCell, judgeCell);
if (halt) log(`HALT: ${halt}. No new trials will start.`);

// ---------- Top-up ----------
phase('Top-up');
const graded = t => t.status === 'completed' && !t.void && t.categoryOk !== undefined;
const bothOk = t => t.categoryOk && t.priorityOk;
const isSplit = c => {
  const g = (c.trials ?? []).filter(graded);
  const pass = g.filter(bothOk).length;
  return g.length > 0 && pass > 0 && pass < g.length;
};
let topUpLeft = C.topUpMaxTotal;
const topCells = [];
if (!halt) {
  for (const c of done.filter(isSplit)) {
    const n = Math.min(C.topUpPerCell, topUpLeft);
    if (n <= 0) { skipped.push({ what: `top-up ${c.key}`, reason: 'top-up cap' }); log(`SKIP top-up ${c.key}: top-up cap reached`); continue; }
    topUpLeft -= n;
    const start = Math.max(0, ...c.trials.map(t => t.trial)) + 1;
    topCells.push({ config: c.config, ticket: c.ticket, key: c.key, start, n, trials: [], topUp: true });
  }
}
log(`Top-up: ${topCells.length} split cells, ${C.topUpMaxTotal - topUpLeft} extra trials.`);
if (topCells.length) {
  const extra = await pipeline(topCells, runTrials, gradeCell, judgeCell);
  for (const e of extra) {
    const base = done.find(c => c.key === e.key);
    if (base && e.trials) base.trials.push(...e.trials.map(t => ({ ...t, topUp: true })));
  }
}

// ---------- Synthesis ----------
phase('Synthesis');
const all = done.flatMap(c => (c.trials ?? []).map(t => ({ ...t, config: c.config, ticket: c.ticket, key: c.key })));
const rate = (xs, f) => (xs.length ? +(xs.filter(f).length / xs.length).toFixed(3) : null);
const mean = (xs, f) => (xs.length ? +(xs.reduce((s, x) => s + (f(x) ?? 0), 0) / xs.length).toFixed(2) : null);

function stats(name, pick) {
  const ts = all.filter(t => t.config === name && pick(t));
  const completed = ts.filter(t => t.status === 'completed');
  const valid = completed.filter(graded);
  const judged = valid.filter(t => t.tonePass !== undefined);
  return {
    trialsRun: ts.length,
    completed: completed.length,
    voided: completed.filter(t => t.void).length,
    harnessErrors: ts.filter(t => t.status === 'harness_error').length,
    rateLimited: ts.filter(t => t.status === 'rate_limited').length,
    graded: valid.length,
    categoryAcc: rate(valid, t => t.categoryOk),
    priorityAcc: rate(valid, t => t.priorityOk),
    bothAcc: rate(valid, bothOk),
    tonePass: rate(judged, t => t.tonePass),
    toneMean: mean(judged, t => t.toneScore),
    meanRuntimeMs: mean(completed, t => t.runtimeMs),
    meanToolCalls: mean(completed, t => t.toolCalls),
    meanToolErrors: mean(completed, t => t.toolErrors),
    meanInputTokens: mean(completed, t => t.inputTokens),
    meanOutputTokens: mean(completed, t => t.outputTokens),
    costUsd: +ts.reduce((s, t) => s + (t.costUsd ?? 0), 0).toFixed(2),
  };
}
// Planned trials are compared with the prediction. Top-ups lean toward split cells, so they are reported apart.
const summary = Object.fromEntries(C.configs.map(k => [k, {
  planned: stats(k, t => !t.topUp),
  topUp: stats(k, t => t.topUp),
}]));

const failing = all.filter(t => graded(t) && (!bothOk(t) || t.tonePass === false));
const odd = all.filter(t => t.void || t.status !== 'completed' || t.gradeMissing);
const failures = (!failing.length && !odd.length) ? { types: [], notes: 'no failing, voided, or errored trials' } : await agent([
  `You analyse failures from the triage eval (${RR}). Configs: ${C.configs.join(', ')}.`,
  `You may read the run files listed below, spe/evals/tasks/answers.json, the tickets under ${C.ticketDir}, and spe/failures.md.`,
  'Read spe/failures.md first. Put an existing F number in existingId when a failure matches one. Do not assign new F numbers.',
  'Group the failing trials into failure types. Give each type a name, kind, what happened, how to spot it, the trial keys it was seen in, the configs it hit, and a proposed fix.',
  'Treat voided trials, harness errors, and missing grades as harness or grader kinds, not agent failures.',
  'Do not change any file. Do not read spe/predictions/.',
  halt ? `The run halted early: ${halt}. Say what the halt means for these results.` : 'The run did not halt.',
  `Failing trials (${failing.length}, first 80 shown):`,
  ...failing.slice(0, 80).map(t => `- ${t.key} t${t.trial} ${t.outPath} category=${t.categoryOk} priority=${t.priorityOk} tone=${t.tonePass ?? 'n/a'}${t.toneReason ? ` (${t.toneReason})` : ''}`),
  `Voided, errored, or ungraded trials (${odd.length}, first 40 shown):`,
  ...odd.slice(0, 40).map(t => `- ${t.key} t${t.trial} status=${t.status} void=${t.void ?? 'no'} error=${t.error ?? ''}`),
].join('\n'), { label: 'failure analysis', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: FAILURE_SCHEMA, model: C.model });

const shortCells = done
  .map(c => ({ key: c.key, valid: (c.trials ?? []).filter(t => !t.topUp && graded(t)).length }))
  .filter(c => c.valid < C.trialsPerCell);
const critic = await agent([
  `You are the completeness critic for the triage eval (${RR}). Read only the JSON below. Do not open files.`,
  `Plan: configs ${C.configs.join(', ')}, ${cells.length / C.configs.length} tickets, ${C.trialsPerCell} trials per cell, top-up up to ${C.topUpPerCell} per split cell and ${C.topUpMaxTotal} total, spend cap $${C.spendCapUsd}.`,
  'List every gap between the plan and what ran. Check cells short of planned valid trials, missing tone scores, budget skips, voids, harness errors, grader errors, and the halt state.',
  'Add a warning that the tone judge is the same model family as the agent.',
  'Set complete to true only when every planned cell has its planned valid trials and no halt occurred.',
  JSON.stringify({ summary, shortCells: shortCells.slice(0, 100), shortCellCount: shortCells.length, skipped, leaks, halt, spentUsd: +spentUsd.toFixed(2) }),
].join('\n'), { label: 'completeness critic', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: CRITIC_SCHEMA, model: C.model });

log(`${RR} done. Spent $${spentUsd.toFixed(2)} of $${C.spendCapUsd}. Skipped ${skipped.length}. Leaks ${leaks.length}. Halt: ${halt ?? 'none'}.`);

return {
  round: ROUND,
  halted: halt,
  spentUsd: +spentUsd.toFixed(2),
  spendCapUsd: C.spendCapUsd,
  summary,
  failures,
  critic,
  skipped,
  leaks,
  trials: all.map(t => ({
    key: t.key, trial: t.trial, topUp: !!t.topUp, status: t.status, void: t.void ?? null,
    categoryOk: t.categoryOk ?? null, priorityOk: t.priorityOk ?? null,
    tonePass: t.tonePass ?? null, toneScore: t.toneScore ?? null,
    runtimeMs: t.runtimeMs ?? null, toolCalls: t.toolCalls ?? null, toolErrors: t.toolErrors ?? null,
    inputTokens: t.inputTokens ?? null, outputTokens: t.outputTokens ?? null, costUsd: t.costUsd ?? null,
    outPath: t.outPath,
  })),
};
```

I made four assumptions, which are listed at the top of the script. The ticket count is 50 because the plan says so, even though the original set had 40. The runner command and its JSON output format are assumed. The $40 cap covers triage runs and judge agents. Tickets live under `spe/evals/tasks/tickets/`.
